# PAY.JP DB backup — age recipient (public key).
#
# This file is committed to the repo intentionally: age recipient keys are
# public by design (they only encrypt). The matching private key lives in
# 1Password ("PAY.JP DB Backup - age private key") + a physical paper/USB
# backup in a safe. Private key NEVER touches the VPS in normal operation.
#
# Used by:
#   scripts/ops/offsite-upload.sh — encrypts pg_dump output before B2 upload.
#   scripts/ops/restore-drill.sh  — same (to verify upload integrity round-trip
#                                   uses private key loaded via systemd-creds,
#                                   only during the drill service run).
#
# Rotation: generate a new keypair, replace this file, re-encrypt existing B2
# objects via admin workflow (or accept that old blobs are unreadable by the
# new private key — not a problem for a rolling 30-day retention window).
